Your buyer's due diligence statement is one form. The file behind it — kept for five years, open to inspection — carries your data.

The EUDR Evidence Readiness Review builds that file to survive the inspection, not just the filing:
• geolocation, production period and legality per plot and lot;
• provenance and date of every record;
• gap register with owners and sequence;
• a summary the buyer's compliance team can attach to its own risk assessment.

Scoped on your actual supplier base and export volume. Written proposal after a scope assessment.

Details: https://www.villanovaesg.com/eudr-evidence-readiness-review/

Advisory review — not a DDS, not certification.

#SupplierEvidence #EUDR #CFO

"Supplier shall provide evidence of compliance upon request." Signed. Filed. Never tested against the file.

The Contract Clause Risk Review tests it before the buyer does:
• clause-by-clause map of every evidence, audit, cooperation and termination obligation;
• for each one: what your file proves today — fact, interpretation, hypothesis;
• the clauses that are termination triggers waiting for a bad quarter;
• a short list of what to fix or renegotiate, for your counsel.

We do not replace your lawyers. We give them the evidence picture they do not have.

Details: https://www.villanovaesg.com/contract-clause-risk-review-eu-facing-suppliers/

